      "created_at": "2026-03-20T18:36:59Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-20T18:36:59Z",
      "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rikosellic/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rikosellic\">@rikosellic</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Do we have APIs like <code class=\"notranslate\">view</code> on the arc? To me it seems more convenient to have something like <code class=\"notranslate\">some_arc@.data</code> so that we can add specs for functions that open <code class=\"notranslate\">arc</code> and borrow its inner data.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm asking it because some code uses <code class=\"notranslate\">Arc</code> for thread-safe accesses to, e.g., DMAs. Without something like <code class=\"notranslate\">view</code> it might not be possible to write specs for some functions in <code class=\"notranslate\">mm::dma</code>.</p>",
      "body_text": "@rikosellic\nDo we have APIs like view on the arc? To me it seems more convenient to have something like some_arc@.data so that we can add specs for functions that open arc and borrow its inner data.\nI'm asking it because some code uses Arc for thread-safe accesses to, e.g., DMAs. Without something like view it might not be possible to write specs for some functions in mm::dma.",
      "body": "@rikosellic\r\n\r\nDo we have APIs like `view` on the arc? To me it seems more convenient to have something like `some_arc@.data` so that we can add specs for functions that open `arc` and borrow its inner data.\r\n\r\nI'm asking it because some code uses `Arc` for thread-safe accesses to, e.g., DMAs. Without something like `view` it might not be possible to write specs for some functions in `mm::dma`.",
