      "created_at": "2026-03-23T03:10:58Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-23T03:10:58Z",
      "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hiroki-chen/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hiroki-chen\">@hiroki-chen</a> If you mean <code class=\"notranslate\">Arc</code> from Rust std, you do not need any extra method to access its value in spec mode. Verus has special treatment for <code class=\"notranslate\">Rc</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">Arc</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Box</code>, which allows you to do things like this:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"use vstd::prelude::*;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nverus!{\n    \n    fn main(){\n        let p = Arc::&lt;usize&gt;::new(5);\n        assert(p==5);\n    }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">use vstd::prelude::*;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nverus!{\n    \n    fn main(){\n        let p = Arc::&lt;usize&gt;::new(5);\n        assert(p==5);\n    }\n}\n</code></pre></div>",
      "body_text": "@hiroki-chen If you mean Arc from Rust std, you do not need any extra method to access its value in spec mode. Verus has special treatment for Rc, Arc and Box, which allows you to do things like this:\nuse vstd::prelude::*;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nverus!{\n    \n    fn main(){\n        let p = Arc::<usize>::new(5);\n        assert(p==5);\n    }\n}",
      "body": "@hiroki-chen If you mean `Arc` from Rust std, you do not need any extra method to access its value in spec mode. Verus has special treatment for `Rc`, `Arc` and `Box`, which allows you to do things like this:\r\n```\r\nuse vstd::prelude::*;\r\nuse std::sync::Arc;\r\n\r\nverus!{\r\n    \r\n    fn main(){\r\n        let p = Arc::<usize>::new(5);\r\n        assert(p==5);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
